Stundenplan MD: third-party material
====================================

Icons
  Files:    app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_settings.xml (settings button), ic_menu.xml (drawer),
            ic_group.xml, ic_person.xml and ic_groups.xml (events shared with friends: 2, 1 and 3+), ic_add.xml (add a friend), ic_share.xml
            (share my plan as a file), ic_qr_code_2.xml (show my plan as a QR code),
            ic_qr_code_scanner.xml (scan a QR code), ic_file_open.xml (pick a friend's file),
            ic_edit.xml (rename a friend), ic_delete.xml (remove a friend), ic_close.xml (close),
            ic_warning.xml (the QR code leaves details out), ic_favorite.xml and
            ic_favorite_filled.xml (favorite friends: "favorite", fill 0 and fill 1),
            ic_chevron_left.xml and ic_chevron_right.xml (back to this week / today; version list),
            ic_arrow_drop_down.xml (the "Ausblenden" menu button),
            ic_list.xml ("format_list_bulleted", version overview), ic_download.xml (install an
            update), ic_open_in_new.xml (actions that leave the page),
            ic_schedule.xml (time picker button)
  Source:   Material Symbols, Outlined, weight 400, 24px, by Google
            https://fonts.google.com/icons
            https://github.com/google/material-design-icons
            (symbols/android/<name>/materialsymbolsoutlined/<name>_24px.xml)
  License:  Apache License, Version 2.0
            https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
  Changes:  the theme-attribute tint was removed and the fill color set to black so the
            app can tint it per theme. The path data is unchanged (ic_list, ic_download and
            ic_open_in_new: taken from the SVG, whose viewBox starts at y = -960, so the path sits
            in a group moved down by 960).

  The web app (web/) uses the same path data, unchanged, as inline SVG (web/src/iconPaths.ts):
            add, chevron_left, chevron_right, close, delete, favorite, favorite_filled, file_open,
            group, menu, qr_code_2, qr_code_scanner, settings, share, warning.

Only these icons are included; the app has no dependency on any icon library. All other
icons are drawn from scratch (app/src/main/java/de/luwify/stundenplanmd/ui/Icons.kt).

Libraries (linked into the app, unmodified)
  ZXing core 3.5.4 (com.google.zxing:core): QR code encoding and decoding.
            https://github.com/zxing/zxing
            License: Apache License, Version 2.0
  CameraX 1.6.2 (androidx.camera: camera-core, camera-camera2, camera-lifecycle,
            camera-compose): camera preview and frames for scanning QR codes.
            https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/camera
            License: Apache License, Version 2.0
  Other AndroidX and Kotlin libraries (Compose, Material 3, DataStore, kotlinx.serialization,
  kotlinx.coroutines): Apache License, Version 2.0.

The theme system (app/src/main/java/de/luwify/stundenplanmd/ui/theme/) is taken from
Mensa MD by the same author and adapted; it is not third-party material.

Web app (web/, bundled into the static page, unmodified)
  Preact 10 (preact): UI.  https://preactjs.com  License: MIT
  pako 2.1.0 (pako): raw deflate/inflate for the share format in the JS build of :core.
            https://github.com/nodeca/pako  License: MIT and Zlib
  jsQR 1.4.0 (jsqr): QR code decoding from camera frames.
            https://github.com/cozmo/jsQR  License: Apache License, Version 2.0
  ZXing for JS 0.21.3 (@zxing/library): QR code encoding as the app's ZXing, and the read-back check of
            one code (encoder version/mask choice and finder pattern selection aligned with ZXing 3.5).
            https://github.com/zxing-js/library  License: Apache License, Version 2.0
  Kotlin standard library and kotlinx.serialization (JS build of :core): Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Tests only (not shipped): Playwright (Apache 2.0), Vite and TypeScript (MIT / Apache 2.0), ZXing javase 3.5.4
  (Apache 2.0) for the Android-side QR checks.
